# AGENTS.md

Shared agent instructions for this project.

This file is the host-neutral instruction surface. Codex reads `AGENTS.md` for
project instructions, and OpenCode reads the same file (falling back to
`CLAUDE.md` when it is absent) and can also load it through the `instructions`
key in `opencode.json`. One file serves both hosts — do not create a second
per-host copy, or the two will drift.

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`. When a rule must hold for every host, state it
here and reference this file from `CLAUDE.md` rather than duplicating it.

## Project Conventions

- Conversation language: {{.ConversationLanguageName}}
- Development methodology: {{.DevelopmentMode}}
- Specifications live under `.moai/specs/`
- Project documentation lives under `.moai/project/`

## Development Workflow

This project follows a three-phase specification-driven workflow.

| Phase | Purpose | Primary artifact |
|-------|---------|------------------|
| plan  | Capture requirements and acceptance criteria before code | `.moai/specs/<SPEC-ID>/spec.md` |
| run   | Implement against the specification, test-first | source files plus tests |
| sync  | Update documentation and close the specification | `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md` |

Work from the specification. When the specification is unclear or appears to
conflict with the code, stop and report the conflict instead of guessing.

## Quality Expectations

- Write or update a test for every behavior change.
- Keep the existing style of any file you modify; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Change only what the task asks for. Leave adjacent code alone.
- Run the project's test and lint commands before declaring work complete, and
  report the actual command output rather than asserting success.

## Language Support

The toolchain detects the project language from the files present in the
repository and runs the matching test, lint, and format commands. The following
languages are supported equally:

`go`, `python`, `typescript`, `javascript`, `rust`, `java`, `kotlin`, `csharp`,
`ruby`, `php`, `elixir`, `cpp`, `scala`, `r`, `flutter`, `swift`

A language marker that is absent simply means those checks are skipped.

## Host Notes

Support levels differ per host. Run `moai host matrix --json` to see the
current event mapping, and `moai host matrix --features --json` to see the
capability-group mapping. Each non-native mapping carries a degradation note
explaining what is approximated and a source field recording the evidence.

Hooks are wired per host:

- Claude Code reads `.claude/settings.json`.
- Codex reads `.codex/hooks.json`. Codex loads that project layer only when the
  project is trusted, so hook delivery is native but trust-conditional.
- OpenCode loads `.opencode/plugins/`, which forwards supported events to the
  same shared hook scripts.
